## Context
Nomination from the sen-causal-reading session (2026-10-15). The author wants
the project's annotated bibliography (which sources are in `docs/`, their
Zotero keys, read/unread status, verified page quotations) to live in project
memory: verifications as journal entries, a consolidated topic file as the
bibliography. Dream's pruning and merging may condense a quotation or a folio,
which is exactly the content that must survive: a plausible wrong locator is
the costly failure (`rules/zotero.md`).

The need was nominated by the sen-causal-reading project. The harness author
confirmed the following solution in the harness discussion on 2026-10-15:
no "sources" special case in roar (a verification is a significant fact like
any other) nor in dream; one general clause in dream covers every verified
quotation, whatever the project. This is an explicit harness decision rather
than a policy inferred from the originating project's experience.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `skills/dream/SKILL.md` states that a quotation verified on the page,
      with its locator (page, folio, note number), is carried verbatim into
      topics and never paraphrased, condensed or merged away; a conflict
      between two recorded locators is kept as an unresolved contradiction.
- [ ] No new section, no source-specific branch in roar or dream.
- [ ] Skill tests updated if they pin dream's wording; `make check` passes.

## Raid Imagine — 2026-10-15
Imagine: fresh author-revalidated premise. Add one general clause under Merging; no new section, source-specific branch or Roar change. No wording-pin test needed.

## Raid Plan — 2026-10-15
Actions: insert general verbatim quote/locator clause into current Merging bullet. Verification: semantic diff inspection and make check; no tautological wording test. Paths: skills/dream/SKILL.md plus own ticket. Dependency: complete before 1105 renames skill.

